[[File:Harpie Bug Swarm icon.png|left]]
'''Harpie bug swarms''' are mid-level [[slayer monsters]] that require a [[Slayer]] level of 33 to kill. A [[lit bug lantern]], which requires a [[Firemaking]] level of 33 to light, is required to damage these [[monsters]] (the lantern '''must''' be lit ''and'' equipped). If you do not have 33 Firemaking, you cannot be assigned harpie bug swarms as a [[Slayer task]].{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/914564835446284288|date=1 October 2017|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/102797|archivedate=25 May 2020|quote=I think all three of the checks you list are still in effect on the creatures in question. Reducing requirements tends not to be popular.}} 

Harpie bug swarms should be an easy task for well-equipped mid-level players; their abundance as well as the fact that they remain aggressive to players until level 93 combat makes this task very click-easy. As harpie bug swarms are ''very'' accurate, and will often hit for up to 6 [[Hitpoints]], it is advisable to have [[Defence]] levels from 40-50+ and to bring [[food]] appropriate for the player's level, such as [[lobster]]s. Another option is to keep [[Protect from Melee]] up and recharge prayer at the relatively nearby altars.

It is recommended to bring [[nature rune]]s while slaying this monster since it has many drops that can be [[High Level Alchemy|alched]] to free up [[inventory]] spaces, and [[fire rune]]s are frequently dropped from this monster.

