===Colossal Wyrm Remains===
* (Recommended) Building a [[Quetzal Transport System|quetzal landing site]] at [[Colossal Wyrm Remains]] opens up a very convenient, quick shortcut to a bank at [[Auburnvale]] and a prayer altar at [[The Teomat]].
* The closest fairy ring is {{Fairycode|ajp}}, requiring you to run south across the open savannah, mostly free of enemies and obstacles.
* Alternatively, it's possible to reach the location from the [[Hunter Guild]] bank or [[Civitas illa Fortis]].

With an appropriate method of transport, this location is very accessible, offers several [[safespot]]s, and is free of dangers associated with Karamja (eliminating the need for an [[antipoison]]).

===Tai Bwo Wannai===

* The closest [[fairy ring]] is {{Fairycode|dkp}}, although you will need to run south, past [[the Shaikahan]] and [[aggressive]] [[jogre]]s, use the log [[shortcut]] to cross the river and then run north. Fairy ring {{Fairycode|ckr}} can also be used, though it's further to the south.
* A [[Tai bwo wannai teleport]] scroll will take you to the nearby village, just south-west of the swarms.
* You can also use the [[Ardougne cloak]]'s teleport to the monastery, run north-east to [[Captain Barnaby]], take the boat to [[Brimhaven]] and run south and east to reach the swarms.
* If the player's [[house]] is in [[Brimhaven]], you can [[Teleport to House]], then walk south to the mainland, then east.
* If the player's [[house]] is in [[Rimmington]], you can [[Teleport to House]], walk west to the ship, then pay 30 coins to travel to [[Brimhaven]] and walk south to the mainland, then east.
* You can also use a [[ring of dueling]] and take the [[Al Kharid]] [[gnome glider]] to the crashed Karamja one, which is slightly slower than the fairy rings.
* With 53 [[Agility]], 21 [[Strength]], 42 [[Ranged]], and any [[crossbow (weapon)|crossbow]] and a [[mithril grapple]], use the Karamja teleport option on a charged [[amulet of glory]], run south-west, and use the grapple agility shortcut. This is faster than any other travel method, but losing an inventory space for the crossbow if not ranging (or the grapple if ranging) may not be appealing to some players.

Completion of [[Tai Bwo Wannai Trio]] enables the use of the nearby [[Tribal Statue]] to recharge prayer points.

There are two [[safespot]]s: one between the two trees to the south behind the small jungle plant, and another to the north on the beaches of the fairy ring (DKP). Players can set up a cannon to range or melee 2+ swarms to the west, but will need runes to [[telegrab]] any desired drops. You can use a [[dwarf multicannon]] in this location, but you have to equip the bug lantern for the cannon to deal damage.

It is highly recommended to bring [[antipoison]] due to the presence of other aggressive, poisonous creatures.

[[File:Harpie bug swarm cannon spot.png|thumb|Cannon semi-safespot for faster kills. ]]

